From e1cc82368dfc9358fc16dd320314067315fad26b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ma-abc123 <abc12302019@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 15:50:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] feat(sf32lb52): sync LCPU patches to upstream, evidence
 capture, self-heal hardening

Per root-cause review: Hardware Error code=0 is the LCPU firmware's
fatal/assert exit.  The local rev_b patch predates two public SiFli-SDK
fixes that match the symptom (2026-04 'fix 52X ble connection update
dump issue' 068fb1c2, 2026-07 'fix 52 bt controller ld stop assert'
f8e025ea): local patch bin 1308B/list 28 (len 0x68) vs upstream
6328B/list 58 (len 0xE0); legacy lcpu_patch.c resynced as well
(patch.h unchanged, no ABI drift).

- lcpu_patch_rev_b.c / lcpu_patch.c: synced to upstream HEAD
  (sha256 e30fcf66.. / f4f8ed68..)
- sf32lb52_lcpu_boot.c: boot log of revid and selected patch path;
  sf32lb52_lcpu_boot_dump_evidence() dumps the LCPU assert record and
  config words before the self-heal clears them
- sf32lb52_bth4.c: exported sf32lb52_bth4_controller_restart() (deinit
  -> init -> RX callback re-registration -> enable; controller_init
  clears the adapter env so the callback must be re-registered) and
  made the self-heal call it for evidence capture
- sf32lb52_ble_bridge.c: conn callbacks re-registered per host
  generation (bt_disable_mc -> bt_dev_free wipes conn_ctx, a static
  'registered' guard left rebuilt hosts deaf); started flag rolled
  back on bt_enable failure; recovery stops on the first failed step
  instead of proceeding with undefined state; connection reference
  unref'd before host cleanup; hw-error rate limit moved into
  take_hw_error() so a gated event stays pending instead of being
  dropped (and zero last_recover_sec no longer swallows the first
  recovery during the first 10s of uptime)
